{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/1500162-tc-adventure-backers-pdf","id":1500162,"title":"TC Adventure! Backers PDF!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: Adventure!"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-12-19T20:41:13-08:00","id":1500162,"title":"TC Adventure! Backers PDF!","content":"By Monday Meeting Notes -<br /> <br /> 'At Press<br /> TC: Adventure! \u2013 Backer PDF going out to Backers this week'<br /> <br /> \ud83c\udf89\ud83e\udd73\ud83c\udf7e<br /> <br /> Topic for finding errors and talk on PDF. \ud83d\ude0e","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-22T13:07:40-08:00","id":1500395,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">I've only just glanced at the PDF, but I already see one errata suggestion I'll be submitting, but hold little hope it'll be implemented, since I submitted the same issue back during the Kickstarter errata pass, and they don't seem to have changed a single word. I even started a thread on the topic back then: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1445150-adventure-era-ism-query\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...-era-ism-query</a><br /> <br /> tl;dr - Pages 248 - 252 cover the seven evils &quot;Isms&quot; of the Adventure! era, providing broad overviews of why they're wrong as well as details regarding specific atrocities committed by adherents...of six out of the seven. The final evil &quot;Ism&quot; of Socialism appears to be the most awesome thing of all time since it is all about taking power from the rich and giving it to the poor. They don't write a single negative thing about the practice beyond stating, &quot;the nation of Mongolia followed the Soviet model, and <i><u>after a violent uprising</u></i>, established the Mongolian People\u2019s Republic&quot;, making no mention that early 20th century socialist movements resulting in at least 6.5-20 million deaths (detailed in my linked thread). Four words out of over 250.<br /> <br /> tl;dr 2 - If they're not going to say a single bad thing about socialism, why is it even listed alongside anti-Semitism, classism, fascism, heterosexism (homophobia), racism, and sexism? I'd rather they cut the section entirely than whitewash forty years of detention camps, mass starvation, and acts of genocide.</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-22T16:10:59-08:00","id":1500406,"title":"","content":"As the book accurately calls out the Holodomor as a Soviet manufactured famine that killed millions by the book\u2019s setting of 1934, I\u2019m not seeing the problem. No the \u201csocialism\u201d entry doesn\u2019t discuss the future death toll of Marxist-Leninist-Maoist regimes, but the entry under \u201cFascism\u201d doesn\u2019t discuss what\u2019s coming either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-22T18:05:59-08:00","id":1500410,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/1500162-tc-adventure-backers-pdf?p=1500406#post1500406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As the book accurately calls out the Holodomor as a Soviet manufactured famine that killed millions by the book\u2019s setting of 1934, I\u2019m not seeing the problem. No the \u201csocialism\u201d entry doesn\u2019t discuss the future death toll of Marxist-Leninist-Maoist regimes, but the entry under \u201cFascism\u201d doesn\u2019t discuss what\u2019s coming either.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, the Fascism entry doesn't list atrocities or death tolls, but it does use language such as:</span></span><ul><li><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Benito Mussolini, a former soldier and socialist, and his fascists <b>took advantage</b> by siding not with workers but with businesses.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">His Blackshirts <b>attacked laborers and peasants</b> in the name of law and order.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Mussolini then <b>ordered his people to seize control</b> of several government buildings, effectively <b>holding the nation hostage</b>.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Fascists believe liberal democracies have failed humankind and seek the complete mobilization of society under a single <b>totalitarian one-party state</b>.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">To handle armed conflicts and economic difficulties, a single leader leads fascists \u2014<b> a dictator</b> able to wield unilateral authority. </span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Fascism believes <b>violence is a means to an end</b></span></span></li> </ul><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">With writing like that, it is obvious why Fascism is listed as one of the era's seven evil Isms. And there is no need to address future socialist atrocities when my Kickstarter period forum post called out four distinct atrocities from prior to the game's &quot;now&quot; of 1934.<br /> <br /> Now let us consider Socialism as portrayed by this PDF. I had to do a FIND word search to locate the Holodomor reference. It wasn't in the Socialist entry for &quot;Isms&quot;, nor did it mention how Holodomor was specifically tied to socialism.<br /> <br /> The words socialism and socialist appear a grand total of 17 times in the book. Let us look at the context of each appearance:<br /> <br /> pg. 8 - Socialism<br /> <br /> [context: An index entry.]<br /> <br /> <br /> pg. 83 - The Bolsheviks, the largest and most influential socialist party in Russia, took matters into their own hands.<br /> <br /> [context: In response to food riots, the Russian government collapses. Various factions fight it out for a few years and the Bolsheviks win. The socialists don't seem bad.]<br /> <br /> <br /> pg. 83 - The winter of 1922 gave birth to the Union of Soviet Socialist Republics.<br /> <br /> [context: Reads like a wiki entry. The socialists still don't seem bad. The next few paragraphs mention bad stuff, but pins the blame directly on Lenin and NPC Marko Burakov rather than socialism.]<br /> <br /> <br /> pg. 83 - Caught between a fascist West and a communist East, Eastern Europe is a patchwork of competing ideologies with democracies, socialists, and dictators all vying for control.<br /> <br /> [context: Reads like another wiki entry. The socialists still don't seem bad.]<br /> <br /> <br /> pg. 84 - Post-war Austria consists of various political camps, socialist and conservative alike, both of whom control far-ranging power structures and their own parliamentary forces.<br /> <br /> [context: Reads like another wiki entry. The socialists still don't seem bad.]<br /> <br /> <br /> pg. 87 - Many of the leaders in Central America find themselves wrapped up in the coils of United Fruit, while fighting against a rising socialist tide. Drawing aid from their Euro-American corporate allies, they each try to apply their boots to the necks of their people,<br /> <br /> [context: So the people who are &quot;fighting against a rising socialist tide&quot; are the same ones who &quot;try to apply their boots to the necks of their people&quot;? Why exactly are the socialists the bad guys here, since they're opposing the brutal oppressors?]<br /> <br /> <br /> On to the section named &quot;THE ISMS&quot;:<br /> <br /> pg. 248 - For a setting based in the 1930s, the most prevalent Isms are anti-Semitism, classism, fascism, heterosexism (homophobia), racism, sexism, and socialism.<br /> <br /> [context: Given the nastiness of the first six entries in this list, socialism must be just as bad, right?]<br /> <br /> <br /> pg. 250 - Benito Mussolini, a former soldier and socialist, and his fascists took advantage by siding not with workers but with businesses.<br /> <br /> [context: Mussolini used to be a socialist. He became an evil fascist and did evil fascist things. This does nothing to make socialism look bad.]<br /> <br /> <br /> pg. 252 - Socialism<br /> <br /> [context: This is just the header for the entry on why socialism is supposedly bad.]<br /> <br /> <br /> pg. 252 - The ill treatment of workers during the late nineteenth century led key intellectuals to lay down a set of principles labeled as socialism.<br /> <br /> [context: Reads like another wiki entry. The socialists still don't seem bad.]<br /> <br /> <br /> pg. 252 - Socialism recognizes class struggle \u2014 the conflict between a ruling class that controls the means of production and the working class that are the means of production.<br /> <br /> [context: Reads like another wiki entry. The socialists still don't seem bad.]<br /> <br /> <br /> pg. 252 - Socialism takes power away from the ruling class and distributes it evenly among the working class.<br /> <br /> [context: Reads like another wiki entry. The socialists still don't seem bad.]<br /> <br /> <br /> pg. 252 - Fueled by the belief in fairness and revolution, socialism spread among the working poor of Europe,<br /> <br /> [context: Reads like another wiki entry. The socialists still don't seem bad.]<br /> <br /> <br /> pg. 252 - With the overthrow of Tzar Nicholas II and the formation of the Union of Soviet Socialist Republics in 1922, socialist parties emerged<br /> throughout Europe, the United States, Mexico, Brazil, Argentina, Chile, China, and Indonesia.<br /> <br /> [context: Reads like another wiki entry. The socialists still don't seem bad.]<br /> <br /> <br /> pg. 252 - The United States even elected two Socialist Party members to the U.S. House of Representatives.<br /> <br /> [context: Reads like another wiki entry. The socialists still don't seem bad.]<br /> <br /> <br /> pg. 252 - These socialist groups unified under the Comintern, also known as the Third International, which promised unequivocally to \u201cstruggle by all available means, including armed force, for the overthrow of the international bourgeoisie and the creation of an international Soviet republic as a transition stage to the complete abolition of the state.\u201d<br /> <br /> [context: Reads like another wiki entry. The socialists still don't seem bad.]<br /> <br /> <br /> Aaand, we're done. We've read every direct mention of socialists and socialism in the book and have learned that Vladimir Lenin and some NPC created for this game were bad people. Beyond that, socialism seems historically boring but philosophically awesome. This is a strange conclusion to reach regarding an &quot;Ism&quot; movement which we're specifically warned is a sensitive topic to be handled with care, and that some players may be uncomfortable addressing the issue at their gaming table.<br /> <br /> It is especially ironic that the introductory section to the era's prevailing &quot;Isms&quot; issues goes on to state, &quot;So, it can sometimes do a disservice to the people and cultures who suffered to simply gloss over the ugly parts of history because they make people uncomfortable.&quot; Yes, it is a disservice to people and cultures to gloss over historical ugliness. You know, the way the writers of this book are glossing over the historical ugliness of socialism? Socialism is specifically called out as one of the evil Isms of the era, so I'd expect it to be treated as such in the socialism entry for the Isms section. Why wasn't it?</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-22T18:30:53-08:00","id":1500412,"title":"","content":"Socialism is not a bad thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-22T21:15:03-08:00","id":1500422,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amethyst</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/1500162-tc-adventure-backers-pdf?p=1500412#post1500412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Socialism is not a bad thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>it\u2019s certainly been used as justification for atrocities by tyrannical regimes in their propaganda. And as most socialists around the world were making the mistake of falling for that propaganda in the 30s and supporting Stalin (outliers like Orwell, the Anarchists, and most Jewish Leftists not withstanding), I do see the point in that being worth giving more discussion.<br /> <br /> But you are also certainly correct that while fascism produced nothing but tyranny and atrocities, socialist theory is a more mixed bag historically because in democratic countries helped organize labour movements that radically expanded human rights and living conditions in the late 19th and 20th century, at the same time that it was wielded by authoritarian regimes to commit atrocities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-23T12:06:05-08:00","id":1500464,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amethyst</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/1500162-tc-adventure-backers-pdf?p=1500412#post1500412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Socialism is not a bad thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>And yet the authors gave it a half page entry in the section of the book dedicated to all of the really horrible stuff going on during the Adventure! era, presumably due to the tens of millions of people murdered, imprisoned, or displaced by that period's socialist movements. A political philosophy that purports to champion the poor murdered millions of peasant farmers to steal their land, justifying it by claiming that owning one or two horses to pull a plow was enough to make them wealthy landowners and therefore enemies of the state.<br /> <br /> Except that half page entry is nothing but propagandistic pro-socialist buzzwords that don't say anything bad about it. Honestly, all they needed to get it right was to break that half page into three subsections:<br /> <br /> 1). A wiki style entry on socialist philosophy/ideals.<br /> <br /> 2). A reality check such as, &quot;Despite these stated ideals, socialist movements of the period were as brutal and repressive as their fascist counterparts.&quot;<br /> <br /> 3). Specific examples of socialist movement atrocities, such as The Red Terror (<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red_Terror\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red_Terror</a>) and Stalin's Collectivisation (<a href=\"http://www.mrbuddhistory.com/uploads/1/4/9/6/14967012/textbook_pages_on_collectivisation.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.mrbuddhistory.com/uploads...tivisation.pdf</a>).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-18T17:29:14-08:00","id":1500676,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shepherdboi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/1500162-tc-adventure-backers-pdf?p=1500464#post1500464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> 3). Specific examples of socialist movement atrocities, such as The Red Terror (<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red_Terror\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red_Terror</a>) and Stalin's Collectivisation (<a href=\"http://www.mrbuddhistory.com/uploads/1/4/9/6/14967012/textbook_pages_on_collectivisation.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.mrbuddhistory.com/uploads...tivisation.pdf</a>).</div> </div> </div> </div>These were atrocities because of being the results of dictatorship.<br /> Non because of socialism.<br /> <br /> Socialism, per se, is not bad.<br /> <br /> As Christianity isn't.<br /> The Holy Crusades, the Inquisition = bad.<br /> Christianity = not bad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27462-william-wilson","name":"William Wilson","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-18T17:33:32-08:00","id":1500678,"title":"","content":"Then it shouldn't have been listed among the Isms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-18T17:38:58-08:00","id":1500679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/1500162-tc-adventure-backers-pdf?p=1500678#post1500678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then it shouldn't have been listed among the Isms.</div> </div> </div> </div>Historically, it's been a major political (and ideological) force in the 20's and 30's.<br /> But if the &quot;Isms&quot; are meant to be bad, I guess the term could be changed to Stalinism: a very specific example of government based on socialism. But not socialism in itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27462-william-wilson","name":"William Wilson","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-18T17:43:42-08:00","id":1500680,"title":"","content":"Or Communism, possibly with a note that it's a misnomer and that what's called Communism is more properly referred to as Stalinism. <br /> <br /> But it's too late now; the text is already finalized, and we're stuck with a series of Isms, every other one being \u201cthis is a real problem, and you shouldn't try to paper over its issues\u201d while this one is \u201cthis has a bad rap, and let's ignore the atrocities that were performed in its name\u201d.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-18T21:17:37-08:00","id":1500697,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>William Wilson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/1500162-tc-adventure-backers-pdf?p=1500676#post1500676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> These were atrocities because of being the results of dictatorship.<br /> Non because of socialism.<br /> <br /> Socialism, per se, is not bad.<br /> <br /> As Christianity isn't.<br /> The Holy Crusades, the Inquisition = bad.<br /> Christianity = not bad.</div> </div> </div> </div>Saying that socialism is not bad per se is like saying fascism is not bad per se, as long as you ignore the nazis and other actual fascists. Theoretically correct, but it is hard to divorce the actions of followers of a political philosophy from the political theories they espouse, and doing so does a disservice to their victims.<br /> <br /> You also claim that these atrocities were the result of the leadership rather than their political beliefs, but that isn't entirely true either. The literal definition of socialism is:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A political and economic theory of social organization which advocates that the means of production, distribution, and exchange should be owned or regulated by the community as a whole. </div> </div> </div>The Union of Soviet Socialist Republics was politically a Federal one-party socialist republic under a totalitarian leader. Their policy of agricultural collectivization was literally an example of consolidating &quot;the means of production, distribution, and exchange&quot; under the control of a government acting on behalf of &quot;the community as a whole.&quot; Their implementation of socialist farming killed tens of millions, as I've already noted. This agricultural policy was just one part of their system of five-year plans, which were ideologically driven (<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ideology_of_the_Communist_Party_of_the_Soviet_Union\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ideolo...e_Soviet_Union</a>).<br /> <br /> The People's Republic of China is a Unitary Marxist-Leninist one-party socialist republic. Their policy of agricultural collectivization was another example of consolidating &quot;the means of production, distribution, and exchange&quot; under the control of a government acting on behalf of &quot;the community as a whole.&quot; The Great Chinese Famine of 1959-1961 killed 15-55 million. It was part of the Great Leap Forward, which was a broader attempt to manage &quot;the means of production, distribution, and exchange&quot; in accordance with Marxist-Leninist political ideology (linked above).<br /> <br /> The Democratic People's Republic of Korea is a Unitary one-party socialist republic under a hereditary totalitarian dictatorship. They have a command economy in line with socialist political theory (linked above), and it has lead to crumbling infrastructure, chronic shortages, and a famine that killed millions.<br /> <br /> If you want to claim that socialism itself holds no blame for this death and misery, could you point to a nation where the government controls the farms and manufacturing and this didn't lead to widespread shortages of food and goods? It seems to me you're conflating such things as &quot;socialized medicine&quot; and &quot;social security&quot; with socialist political doctrine; they're loosely related, but not the same.\u200b Read the doctrine, then read the history of various ideologically driven socialist nations, and you'll see how the atrocities were supported by socialist political theory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}